{name:'Dragon Blood Tree',latin:'Dracaena cinnabari',tag:'SOCOTRA · ISLAND',rarity:'RARE',height:'6–10 m',range:'Socotra archipelago',status:'Vulnerable',era:'Island-adapted lineage',desc:'Its umbrella crown is shaped by intense sunlight and dry island winds; its famous red resin inspired its name.',facts:['Umbrella-shaped crown','Red resin: dragon’s blood','Endemic to Socotra region','Slow growth and drought adapted']},
{name:'Monkey Puzzle',latin:'Araucaria araucana',tag:'ANDES · CONIFER',rarity:'ENDANGERED',height:'30–50 m',range:'Southern Chile & Argentina',status:'Endangered',era:'Gondwanan lineage',desc:'A spiky, architectural conifer with ancient relatives and a highly distinctive silhouette.',facts:['Needle-like rigid leaves','Seeds are edible','National tree of Chile','Fire and habitat loss are threats']},
{name:'Franklin Tree',latin:'Franklinia alatamaha',tag:'USA · LOST WILD',rarity:'EXTINCT WILD',height:'6–10 m',range:'Georgia, USA — cultivated only',status:'Extinct in the wild',era:'18th-century relic',desc:'The species vanished from its natural range; every Franklin tree alive today descends from cultivated material.',facts:['Last wild sighting in 1803','White fragrant flowers','Camellia family','Survives through cultivation']},
